            <ArticleTitle>Transcatheter recanalization of the left main pulmonary artery after four years of complete occlusion.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>81-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A technique for transcatheter &quot;reconstruction&quot; of a completely occluded left pulmonary artery using radiofrequency perforation with subsequent balloon dilation and stent implantation is reported in a 7-year-old child. It is shown that transcatheter radiofrequency perforation can still be effective years after the occlusion of a vessel.</AbstractText>
